COPYRIGHT NOTICE — NO LICENCE IS GRANTED
========================================

Copyright (c) 2026 <OWNER — replace this placeholder with your name or entity>

All rights reserved. No licence is granted by this file. You may not copy,
modify, distribute or use this work except as the copyright holder permits or
the law allows.

Why a placeholder rather than a guess
-------------------------------------

The value of this notice is that it is accurate, and a copyright line naming
the wrong person is worse than one with an obvious blank. Replace the line
above; it is the only edit this file needs.


1. The same posture as the predecessor, for the opposite reason
---------------------------------------------------------------

The predecessor repository (`odl20lite`) also grants nothing, and this one was
asked to match it. The posture is the same; the reason must not be copied,
because it does not apply here and repeating it would be false.

The predecessor withholds a grant because **nobody has established who may give
one**: its first-party code originates with University College London, no rights
statement ever existed in that tree, and an offer that may not be the offeror's
to make is worse than no offer.

This tree withholds a grant because **the owner has not yet decided to give
one**. That is an entirely different thing. The work here is written from public
literature and public standards — the IERS Conventions, published papers,
published format specifications — under a clean-room discipline recorded in
`doc/REWRITE_PLAN.md` and evidenced in every specification's derivation
declaration. Nothing here descends from anyone else's source code.

So: the predecessor *cannot* grant a licence. This tree *can*, and has chosen
not to yet.


2. This is the choice that keeps every option open
---------------------------------------------------

It is worth being explicit that "no grant" is not a restrictive posture here so
much as an undecided one, and it is the only starting position that forecloses
nothing:

  * a grant can be added at any time, and made retroactive if wanted;
  * a grant once published is, in practice, impossible to withdraw;
  * publication, sale, exclusive licensing, open-sourcing and giving it away
    all remain available from here, and each remains the owner's sole decision.

Starting permissive would have given that away for nothing, before anyone knows
which of those is wanted.


3. What this file does not reach
---------------------------------

Third-party components, when there are any. There are none today — this tree is
currently specifications, a provenance ledger and a set of frozen oracle
measurements. The dependencies the plan anticipates (ERFA under BSD, CALCEPH
under CeCILL-B) keep their own terms, and `PROVENANCE.md` carries the dependency
register that records each one and, where a component is multi-licensed, which
option was chosen.

The measurements under `oracle/` are observations of what a program printed,
recorded with the commands and input hashes that produced them. Facts about what
software did are not the property of whoever wrote the software.


4. On the name
---------------

The plan's original guidance for the project name was "anything that is not an
echo of ODL/SGNL", to keep structural distance for the ownership story. The
owner chose `odl/self_built`, which overrides that guidance deliberately: it
names the problem domain rather than claiming descent, and `self_built` states
the point of the exercise in the name itself. The concern the original guidance
was protecting against is recorded here rather than silently dropped, so that a
later decision to rename is an informed one.


5. If you are reading this because you want to use the work
-------------------------------------------------------------

Ask the copyright holder. Unlike the predecessor, where the answer to "who can
give me permission?" is genuinely unresolved, here there is someone who can
answer.
